.TH ISOCMD 1 "October 2026" "Iso Commander 7.9.3" "Iso-Commander Manual"

.SH NAME
Iso Commander (isocmd) \- A single binary command-line utility for managing .iso files and converting image formats.

.SH DESCRIPTION
Iso Commander (isocmd) is a single binary command-line utility for managing .iso files and converting various image formats to .iso using multi-threaded processing.

.SH NON-INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.SS Version
.TP 16
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show program version.
.SS Actions
.TP 16
.B mount
Mount one or more ISO files or scan directories for ISO files and mount them (requires root).
.TP 16
.B umount/unmount
Unmount specified ISO mount points. Without paths, or with \fBall\fR as the only path, scan /mnt/ISOs and attempt to unmount all contained mount points (requires root).
.TP 16
.B c2iso
Convert supported images to ISO files. Accepts individual image files and directories to scan. Supported formats are BIN, IMG, CCD, MDF, NRG, CHD, DAA and GBI.
.TP 16
.B w2usb
Write ISO files to removable USB flash devices (requires root). Arguments beginning with \fB/dev/\fR are target devices.
.br
All arguments are validated before any device is touched. Only raw devices are accepted, not device partitions.
.SS Action Flags
.TP 16
.B \-\-silent
Suppress informational messages, warnings and progress output. Critical errors will still be displayed.
.TP 16
.B \-d\fIN\fR
Maximum recursion depth when scanning directories for ISO files or convertible images (default: unlimited). A depth of 0 scans only the specified directories.
.br
Ignored by \fBw2usb\fR, which does not scan directories, and by \fBumount/unmount\fR, which only require surface scans.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TS
tab(@);
lb l.
isocmd mount /path/to/file1.iso /path/to/file2.iso@Mount specific ISOs
isocmd mount /path/to/dir@Mount all ISOs in a directory
isocmd mount \-d2 /path/to/dir@Mount ISOs up to depth 2
isocmd mount \-\-silent /path/to/file.iso@Mount an ISO with minimal output
@
isocmd umount /mnt/ISOs/mountedISO1 /mnt/ISOs/mountedISO2@Unmount specific ISO mount points
isocmd umount /mnt/ISOs/mountedISO1@Unmount a specific ISO mount point
isocmd umount@Unmount all ISO mount points under /mnt/ISOs
isocmd umount all@Unmount all ISO mount points under /mnt/ISOs
isocmd umount \-\-silent@Unmount all ISO mount points with minimal output
@
isocmd c2iso /path/to/image.bin@Convert a BIN image to ISO
isocmd c2iso /path/to/image.mdf /path/to/image.nrg@Convert multiple images to ISO
isocmd c2iso /path/to/image-dir@Convert supported images in a directory
isocmd c2iso \-d2 /path/to/image-dir@Convert images up to depth 2
isocmd c2iso \-\-silent /path/to/image-dir@Convert images with minimal output
@
isocmd w2usb file.iso /dev/sdc@Write one ISO to one USB device
isocmd w2usb file.iso /dev/sdc /dev/sdd@Write one ISO to multiple USB devices
isocmd w2usb file1.iso file2.iso /dev/sdc /dev/sdd@Write file1.iso to sdc and file2.iso to sdd
isocmd w2usb \-\-silent file.iso /dev/sdc@Write an ISO with minimal output
.TE

.SH UI INTERACTIVE OPTIONS AND FEATURES
.TP
.B ManageISO
Mount, unmount, delete, move, copy, and write ISO files to USB (bootable preserved). Requires root for mount/umount/write2usb.

.TP
.B Convert2ISO
Ported from original C tools and utilizes libchdr.
.br
Converts .bin, .img, .chd, .daa, .gbi, .mdf, and .nrg files to .iso.
.br
.sp
.B ccd2iso
(GPL-2.0 or later, Danny Kurniawan and Kerry Harris) \(em converts CloneCD .bin/.img disc images.
.br
.B mdf2iso
(GPL-2.0 or later, Salvatore Santagati) \(em converts Alcohol 120% .mdf disc images.
.br
.B nrg2iso
(GPL-3.0 or later, Grégory Kokanosky) \(em converts Nero Burning ROM .nrg disc images.
.br
.B daa2iso
(GPL-2.0 or later, Luigi Auriemma) \(em converts PowerISO .daa and gBurner .gbi disc images.
.br
.B libchdr
(BSD-3-Clause, MAME project, Romain TISSERAND) \(em decodes Compressed Hunks of Data (.chd) images.
.TP

.B ImportISO
Creates and updates a local ISO database. The database has a maximum file size limit of \fB1MB\fR.

.SH FILTERING
Press \fB/\fR in a list to open the filter prompt. Matching is a plain substring search. The list
updates live as you type (see \fBlive_filter_limit\fR), and Enter applies the filter. Esc or Ctrl+D cancels.
.SS Syntax
.TS
tab(@);
lb l.
;@OR: an entry matches if it satisfies any group
&@AND: within a group, an entry must contain every non-negated term
!@NOT: at the start of a term, excludes entries containing it (applies to the whole query)
\e;@Literal ';'
\e&@Literal '&'
\e!@Literal '!'
\e\e@Literal '\e'
.TE
.PP
AND binds tighter than OR, so \fBping&pong;metal&gear\fR matches entries containing both
\fIping\fR and \fIpong\fR, or both \fImetal\fR and \fIgear\fR.
.br
A term starting with \fB!\fR excludes every entry containing it, in any group:
\fBa;b&!t\fR matches entries with \fIa\fR or \fIb\fR, but never \fIt\fR. A \fB!\fR elsewhere in a
term is literal (use \fB\e!\fR for a leading one).
.br
Empty terms are ignored (\fBa&&b\fR is \fBa&b\fR). A backslash before any
other character is treated as a normal character.

.SS Case sensitivity
Matching is "smart case" per term: a term with no uppercase letters is case-insensitive, and a term
containing at least one uppercase letter is case-sensitive. This applies to negated terms too.
.SS What is matched
With \fBfilenames_only\fR enabled, only filenames are searched. In the umount
list, the mount-point names are searched (without its trailing \fB~hash\fR suffix) unless the full
list is displayed.
.SS Nested filters
Applying a filter while one is already active narrows the current results further. Filters are
re-applied automatically when the list refreshes.

.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is located at \fI~/.config/isocmd/config\fR and uses a \fIkey = value\fR format.
.SS THEME
.TS
tab(@);
l l 1.
base  Default state and input color@charcoal|black|gray|silver|ash|white|steel (Default: white)
skin  Accent color for menus and headers@green|cyan|white|purple|amber|rose|gray|black (Default: white)
theme Color palette for lists and prompts@original|classic|high_contrast|neon|ocean|sunset|forest|
@midnight|mono|retro|crimson|dracula|tokyo|paper|sakura (Default: original)
.TE
.SS GENERAL
.TS
tab(@);
lb l l.
auto_update@Enable background metadata updates on startup@on|off (Default: off)
filenames_only@Show filenames instead of full paths; global override except unmount list@on|off (Default: off)
live_filter_limit@Max list items for live filtering to remain active (0 to disable)@integer >= 0 (Default: 10000)
pagination@Items per page (0 to disable)@integer >= 0 (Default: 25)
.TE
.SS HISTORY
.TS
tab(@);
lb l l.
folder_path_history_lines@Max unique folder paths to persist (0 to disable)@integer (Default: 30)
filter_history_lines@Max unique search filters to persist (0 to disable)@integer (Default: 15)
.TE
.SS DISPLAY
Controls whether lists are shown in \fBfull\fR (detailed) or \fBcompact\fR format.
If \fBfilenames_only\fR is enabled, path details are stripped regardless of these settings.
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
lb lb.
List@Default
_
mount_list@compact
umount_list@full
cp_mv_rm_list@full
write2usb_list@compact
convert2iso_lists@compact

.TE
.SS THREADS
Iso Commander uses a static central thread pool (size = min(hardware_threads, combined_thread_cap)).
.br
Sub-limits draw from this pool; tasks queue if the pool is full.
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
lb l.
combined_thread_cap@Global thread pool limit (Default: 16, takes effect on restart)
thread_cap_for_mount@Max concurrent mounting tasks (Default: 8)
thread_cap_for_umount@Max concurrent unmounting tasks (Default: 8)
thread_cap_for_cp_mv@Max concurrent copy/move tasks (Default: 4)
thread_cap_for_rm@Max concurrent file removal tasks (Default: 8)
thread_cap_for_convert2iso@Max concurrent ISO conversions (Default: 4)
thread_cap_for_database_cleanup@Max concurrent threads for ISO database cleanup (Default: 4)
thread_cap_for_list_sorting@Max concurrent threads for UI list sorting (Default: 2)
thread_cap_for_list_filtering@Max concurrent threads for UI list filtering (Default: 2)
.TE

.SH FILES
.I Note: If run with sudo, these paths are relative to /root/ instead of the user's home directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/isocmd/config
Primary configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/isocmd/database/iso_commander_database.txt
Main ISO metadata database.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/isocmd/database/iso_commander_path_database.txt
Persistent history of accessed folder paths.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/isocmd/database/iso_commander_filter_database.txt
Persistent history of search filter terms.

